  "submitted_text": "Step 1: To convert the decimal number \\(999_{10}\\) to its base six equivalent, we need to repeatedly divide the number by 6 and keep track of the remainders.\n\nStep 2: Divide 999 by 6:\n\\[ 999 \\div 6 = 166 \\text{ remainder } 3 \\]\nSo, the least significant digit (rightmost) is 3.\n\nStep 3: Divide the quotient 166 by 6:\n\\[ 166 \\div 6 = 27 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\nThe next digit is 4.\n\nStep 4: Divide the quotient 27 by 6:\n\\[ 27 \\div 6 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 3 \\]\nThe next digit is 3.\n\nStep 5: Finally, divide the quotient 4 by 6:\n\\[ 4 \\div 6 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\nThe most significant digit (leftmost) is 4.\n\nStep 6: Reading the remainders from bottom to top, the base six representation of \\(999_{10}\\) is \\(4343_6\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{4343_6}",
